2. Free individual use

An individual may use, run, copy and modify the Software without paying a fee
for that individual's own use. This includes personal learning, research,
private self-hosting used only by that individual, personal projects, portfolio
demonstrations, and keeping that individual's own work journals or reports.
An employee or freelancer may independently use the Software to document their
own work, including on a work computer, and may submit or share the resulting
documents with an employer or client without buying a commercial license.
Use on multiple devices by the same individual is permitted.

This permission does not cover deployment or operation by or for an organization,
shared multi-user systems, or commercial distribution or services described in
section 3. The fact that an organization benefits from an individual's exported
report does not by itself make the individual's use a paid use. Merely reimbursing
an individual's device or permitting personal installation does not by itself
constitute organization-wide deployment.

3. Uses requiring a paid commercial license

Before doing any of the following, obtain a separate written commercial license
from MIZHOUCL and pay any fees specified in that agreement:

(a) Centrally deploying, provisioning, administering or operating the Software
    for a company, team or other organization, including batch installation,
    company-provided instances, shared accounts and team-wide infrastructure.
(b) Operating shared or multi-user instances, team dashboards, centralized
    collection of other people's records, or organizational monitoring,
    reporting or management systems based on the Software.
(c) Offering the Software or its functionality to customers or other third
    parties as a hosted service, SaaS, API, managed service or commercial
    product, whether charged directly or monetized through subscriptions,
    advertising, bundled services or other commercial arrangements.
(d) Selling, renting, sublicensing for payment, white-labeling, or bundling the
    Software or modified versions into a commercial product or service.
(e) Providing paid installation, customization, deployment, operation or support
    of the Software for another person or organization.

Independent individuals using their own separate copies and sharing only their
output documents remain covered by section 2. Sharing Software accounts,
instances or centrally managed records is not merely sharing output documents.

No commercial license is granted merely by contacting MIZHOUCL, requesting a
quote, downloading the Software or making an unsolicited payment. Price,
licensed users or deployments, term, support and any additional rights must be
agreed in writing. This license does not set an automatic per-user fee.

